    "# Notebook 03: Model Training and Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "The primary objective of this notebook is to train, evaluate, and compare multiple machine learning models for multiclass disease prediction using the preprocessed healthcare dataset generated in the previous notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "The processed dataset is loaded, split into training and testing sets, and used to train different classification algorithms. Each model is evaluated using multiple performance metrics to determine the most suitable algorithm for deployment in the AI-Powered Healthcare Diagnosis Assistant.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Machine Learning Models Used\n",
    "\n",
    "The following machine learning algorithms are implemented and compared:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Logistic Regression\n",
    "- Random Forest Classifier\n",
    "- Decision Tree Classifier\n",
    "- Gaussian Naive Bayes\n",
    "\n",
    "## Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The performance of each model is evaluated using:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Training Accuracy\n",
    "- Testing Accuracy\n",
    "- Precision\n",
    "- Recall\n",
    "- F1-Score\n",
    "- Training Time\n",
    "\n",
    "## Visualizations Included\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook also includes several visualizations for better model analysis:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Model Accuracy Comparison\n",
    "- Training Time Comparison\n",
    "- Precision, Recall and F1-Score Comparison\n",
    "- Disease Distribution Visualization\n",
    "- Feature Importance Analysis\n",
    "- Final Model Ranking\n",
    "\n",
    "## Outcome\n",
    "\n",
    "After comparing all machine learning models, the best-performing model is selected and saved along with the Label Encoder. These saved files are later used in the Streamlit-based AI Healthcare Diagnosis Assistant for real-time disease prediction."
   ]
  },
